Renault's remanufacturing program recovers components including engines, transmissions, and injection pumps from its dealer network for systematic refurbishment to OEM specifications. Components reach same-as-new condition with comprehensive warranties, retailing at 50-70% of new part pricing. The program reduces water consumption by 88% and energy use by 80% compared to manufacturing equivalents. By creating secondary markets for remanufactured components, Renault extends equipment lifespan while generating service revenue and developing technical expertise in reverse logistics and quality assurance. This automotive-scale remanufacturing demonstrates feasibility for complex mechanical systems in regulated industries.